{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction.identityI_of_inputs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction.identityI_of_inputs","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIReduction.lean#L39-L53","doc":"**Identity I, conditional on the two narrowed inputs.** Let `Emom2 n` be the Plancherel mean\n`E[Σ_c content(c)²]` and `Ehook2 n` be `E[Σ_c h_c²]`. Given\n  * `h_content` : the content second-moment law `Emom2 n = C(n,2) = n(n−1)/2`\n    (Jucys–Murphy / Kerov — no hook-length formula), and\n  * `h_residual` : the elementary residual `Ehook2 n − Emom2 n = n²`,\nIdentity I follows: `Ehook2 n = n(3n−1)/2`. The hook-length formula `f^λ = n!/∏ h_c` is **not**\nused — the dependency is exactly `h_content` and `h_residual`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction.identityI_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIReduction.identityI_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIReduction.lean#L34-L37","doc":"**Arithmetic core of the reduction.** `C(n,2) + n² = n(3n−1)/2`, written with the content\nsecond moment `C(n,2) = n(n−1)/2` in field form. ","signatureChunk":0}]}